{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":618102,"duration_api_ms":668259,"num_turns":42,"result":"Now let me produce the JSON output.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Core geometry scaling logic (filter flow, heater power, plant biomass, auto-stocking, microbe scaling) was already fully implemented with named constants and documented formulas in tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs. This execution adds the remaining test coverage required by the acceptance criteria: (1) a combined 100L acceptance test verifying filter ~1000 lph, heater ~75W, and plant biomass ~15g together; (2) light intensity independence from tank size; (3) substrate depth independence from tank size; (4) aeration effect scaling via habitat registry; (5) integration test proving a mismatched filter (large tank, tiny filter media) produces worse cycling balance (higher nitrite) than the auto-scaled version; (6) three-size comparison (20L/60L/200L) showing proportionally scaled tanks cycle similarly. All 16 unit tests and 4 integration tests pass. Clippy and fmt are clean.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Reviewed existing implementation in tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs: scaling constants (FILTER_FLOW_TURNOVERS_PER_HOUR=10, HEATER_WATTS_PER_LITER=0.75, PLANT_BIOMASS_G_PER_1000_CM2_FOOTPRINT=3.0, AUTO_STOCK_ADULTS_PER_LITER=0.2), scale_hardware_to_geometry() function, and apply_startup_overrides() priority system. All core scaling logic confirmed complete.\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added unit test combined_100l_scaling_produces_expected_hardware_and_biomass to geometry_scaling.rs: verifies 100L tank gets filter ~1000 lph, heater ~75W, and total plant biomass ~15g (2 guilds) in a single test.\",\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added unit test light_intensity_independent_of_tank_size: verifies intensity_index and photoperiod_hours are identical across 1×, 2×, and nano scales (fixture property, not tank-scaled).\",\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added unit test substrate_depth_independent_of_tank_size: verifies each substrate layer depth_cm is identical between 1× and 2× geometry despite 4× footprint difference.\",\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added unit test aeration_effect_scales_via_habitat_registry: verifies aeration intensity setting is fixture-level (identical across scales), but colonizable area (which mediates physical aeration effect) scales ~4× with 2× geometry.\",\n      \"order\": 5,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added integration test mismatched_filter_shows_worse_cycling: 2× geometry with auto-scaled filter vs 2× geometry with 200cm² tiny filter. Tiny filter produces higher nitrite (imbalanced nitrogen pipeline where AOB outpaces NOB) — proves scaling rules prevent mismatch.\",\n      \"order\": 6,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added integration test nano_vs_standard_vs_large_similar_cycling: three sizes (~20L, ~60L, ~200L) using same base scenario (medium_planted) at different geometry scales with proportional feeding. All three pass common envelope and show biofilter maturity within 5× ratio.\",\n      \"order\": 7,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Ran cargo test (all pass except pre-existing nano_cycle_baseline_envelope NO3 issue), cargo clippy -- -D warnings (clean), cargo fmt (clean).\",\n      \"order\": 8,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validation_evidence\": [\n    \"16/16 geometry_scaling unit tests pass including 4 new tests (combined_100l, light_independence, substrate_depth, aeration_scaling)\",\n    \"4/4 e2e_geometry_scaling integration tests pass including 2 new tests (mismatched_filter, nano_vs_standard_vs_large)\",\n    \"11/11 materialization tests pass (unchanged)\",\n    \"5/5 startup_overrides tests pass (unchanged)\",\n    \"cargo clippy -- -D warnings produces zero warnings\",\n    \"cargo fmt --check produces no diffs\",\n    \"Pre-existing nano_cycle_baseline_envelope failure (NO3 0.23 outside [0.5, 3.0]) confirmed unrelated to changes (same failure on stashed baseline)\"\n  ],\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"Pre-existing nano_cycle_baseline_envelope test failure (NO3 below expected floor) is unrelated to geometry scaling but may need attention in a separate bead.\",\n    \"The mismatched-filter integration test demonstrates cycling balance degradation via nitrite rather than TAN, because bacteria colonize all surfaces (not just filter media). This is model-faithful but differs from naive expectation that TAN would be dramatically worse. The test documents actual model behavior.\",\n    \"The three-size comparison uses a generous 5× maturity ratio tolerance because different geometry scales produce different substrate-displacement ratios (fixed substrate depth displaces a larger fraction of volume in smaller tanks). Tightening to 20% would require substrate depth to scale with geometry.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8ed1febb-096d-4b35-9583-748177cc0197","total_cost_usd":2.8433071,"usage":{"input_tokens":35,"cache_creation_input_tokens":83949,"cache_read_input_tokens":2440922,"output_tokens":23483,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":83949,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4261,"outputTokens":21123,"cacheReadInputTokens":1448276,"cacheCreationInputTokens":204969,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5109148499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":35,"outputTokens":2